uestion" "q-333508" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/select "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-333508" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "dependent"] ["text" "independent"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-333508" "field" "field-5" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "dependent"] "category" "ma_explicit_answer" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-79894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ for ${y}_{1}(x)=2x+1$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x-1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-79894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ of two functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ is defined as:\n\n$$\nW({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}|={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${y}_{1}(x)=2x+1$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x-1.$ Therefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =(2x+1){(x-1)}^{′}-(x-1){(2x+1)}^{′} \\\\  & =(2x+1)(1)-(x-1)(2) \\\\  & =2x+1-2x+2 \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-79894" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f31a0fbdf99cfda2ea86e857f382e4d5ec78a2be790cf94c511fd56e9942be3e"} {"question" "q-79894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-79894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "2x-1"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "3x"] ["math" "4x+3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-79894" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-129800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ for ${y}_{1}(x)=x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-129800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ of two functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nW({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}|={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${y}_{1}(x)=x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =(x){(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{′}-(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){(x)}^{′} \\\\  & =x(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-(x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & ={x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-129800" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f31a0fbdf99cfda2ea86e857f382e4d5ec78a2be790cf94c511fd56e9942be3e"} {"question" "q-129800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-129800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "1-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)"] ["math" "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] ["math" "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-129800" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-129797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ for ${y}_{1}(x)=x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {"question" "q-129797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The Wronskian $W({y}_{1},{y}_{2})$ of two functions ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\nW({y}_{1},{y}_{2})=|\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′} & {y}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}|={y}_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have ${y}_{1}(x)=x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W({y}_{1},{y}_{2}) & =(x){(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{′}-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x){(x)}^{′} \\\\  & =(x)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(1) \\\\  & =x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14062380/state.json" "file_sha256" "48bc43d5e6530a4043e3df74cd58c559d2e3e3e7db65742ff7d3e5a0365109f0"} {